# DCO Self + indie driver financial books (Vasanth PRs #62–#64, #67 on his repo).
# 9 chained migrations: ensure_dco_workspace → qualify fix → tag party →
# financial book (4 tables + RPCs) → indie book (4 tables + RPCs) →
# finance visibility → tag no-notes forward → drop legacy overload →
# issue trip scope (workspace/driver/DCO-mode check, one active receivable per trip).
#
# Dependency chain: 1→2→3→4,5,7→6→8→9 (9 needs 4) — apply in listed (ascending) order.
# Functions and tables only; all CREATE OR REPLACE / IF NOT EXISTS / IF EXISTS.
# No destructive DDL; re-applying a completed set is safe (idempotent).
#
# OPERATOR NOTES:
#   Migration #3 (20271101222100) adds a nullable `dco_party_billed numeric` column
#   to `trips` with no default — metadata-only on PG 11+ (no table rewrite, brief lock).
#   It also creates a UNIQUE INDEX on `driver_ledger` (NOT CONCURRENTLY) which holds
#   a ShareLock for the duration of the index build. Apply during a low-traffic window.
#   Before applying, check table size:
#     SELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_total_relation_size('driver_ledger'::regclass));
#
# Prerequisite: prod must already have 20271029223000 (compliance_resubmit, applied via prod-2026-10-29).
# Apply Nihas sets (department-manager-rbac, clear-cancel-reason-on-award) before or alongside —
# they are independent but should be applied in this release.
#
# Apply only via: npm run db:push-set -- prod-2026-11-02-dco   (dry-run first; prod apply needs Vasanth's GO)
# Never via plain `supabase db push` / `npm run db:push`.
#
# Verify before applying:
#   npx jest supabase/migrations/__tests__/prodDcoSelfDriverBooks.set.test.ts \
#            supabase/migrations/__tests__/dcoSelfWorkspaceAndTag.contract.test.ts \
#            supabase/migrations/__tests__/dcoSelfFinancialBook.contract.test.ts \
#            supabase/migrations/__tests__/dcoSelfIssueTripScope.contract.test.ts
# DB guards (disposable or approved database only): supabase/tests/dco_self_issue_trip_scope_guards.sql
